{"author":{"id":"fb9734b7331903226ef3f5df545b960dd5ac64d18b49faee11e8b8e0bd561c91"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1783167798,"nonce":"1ycwKdCameL7HGgVw8vyrkcunfc=","message":"Phase 3 DONE -- fully-streamed proof achieved. Strict all-28 smoke completed end-to-end: ingraph_packs=28, regional_compiled_blocks=0, unavailable_reasons=[], graph_breaks=0, fetches=224 = 28 packs x 8 trunk calls (exactly one H2D per streamed block per pass), image decoded; 80.1s total, steady forward avg 5.83s/pass (transfer-bound: ~11.3 GiB H2D/pass, 90.6 GiB total), DXGI settled 14.08/15.13 GiB. Getting there took three fixes: (a) attach-time pinning must be 0 (pinned weights + packs double-commit since packs use repoint=False; with default auto-pin the packs fail closed as non_pinned_pack); (b) _empty_host_flat now empties the caching host allocator and retries once when pack pinning fails -- the sampler-restore leaves ~12 GiB of pinned D2H staging cached, which otherwise starves cudaHostAlloc; (c) bounce pool must be off (AI_TOOLKIT_BOUNCE_POOL_GIB=0 in the smoke): with packs at 14.07/15.13 GiB the pool pinning live buffers during the sample is what pushed past the shared budget and hard-crashed with cudaErrorMemoryAllocation at the first latent alloc (log ordering was deceptive: the restore line printed during exception unwinding; the crash was BEFORE any denoise step). Remaining DoD items also closed this session: (7,10) tests/test_ingraph_stability.py -- repack (new host tensors, same values) and same-shape repeats cause zero recompiles; depth=2 buffer-reuse hammer, 50 passes x 8 blocks, signed-permutation weights, bitwise-exact; (8) parity vs no-compile eager streamed baseline (same seed/steps/prompts): 15-block mean abs pixel diff 1.8/255 p99=19, all-28 mean 2.1/255 p99=20 max=80 -- consistent with fp8-native _scaled_mm vs dequant eager + Inductor bf16 epilogue rounding. Full tests/ suite 211 passed. Related fixes landed: pinned-weight auto-budget cap now governed by the real DXGI headroom probe, RAM proxies only as fallback (manager._cap_auto_pin_budget + new bounce_pool.dxgi_pinned_headroom; tests in test_pin_budget_caps.py); bounce pool not created when every streamed layer is already pinned (pinned-source bypass makes it redundant and it competes for the same WDDM shared budget). Hand-offs to Phase 6: pack_block_host pins unguarded (must consult the DXGI ledger; over-pinning turns the WDDM slowdown cliff into a hard crash); planner must coordinate attach pinning / bounce pool / packs as one shared-budget consumer set (the three manual knobs above ARE that policy, done by hand); repoint=False duplication means full-pin-at-attach and ingraph packs cannot coexist. Separately filed: f2aceba (order-dependent Quanto pin-accounting test failures in full-suite runs).","files":null}]}